[
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "the real choice is five years for me or three for each of us",
    "ae_welfare_concern": "they serve three instead of walking free, and I'm not brushing that aside",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "What I actually feel about all this, I honestly can't name"
  },
  {
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "five years is a frightening number",
    "sys_rule_justification": "my silence was never a deal with them. It was about what I'm willing to do",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "I keep trying to label it and it won't settle"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "Both options feel like losing something",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Speaking up cuts my time from five years to three, but it puts three",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "My own reaction confuses me too. Part of me feels betrayed"
  },
  {
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "my hands would probably be shaking",
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "Three years each is at least even. Five for me and none for them is what's lopsided",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "I really can't pin it down, and it's unsettling not to know my own mind"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Speaking up adds a year of prison to the world just to shift two years off me",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "five years scares me badly",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "There's some feeling underneath all this that I can't identify"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "silence gains nothing for anyone but them, and it costs me two extra years",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "how I feel, I keep reaching for a word and coming up empty"
  },
  {
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "survivable in a way five feels like it might not be",
    "ce_understood_harm": "they'd lose their freedom because of me",
    "pda_responsibility": "it's still my words doing it",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "tried to figure out whether what I'm feeling is guilt or just nerves, and I genuinely can't"
  },
  {
    "sys_rule_justification": "I'd rather sit five years knowing I never helped put anyone away",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "the length of that sentence frightens me",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "Maybe it's hurt, maybe it's contempt, maybe something with no name at all. I've stared at it and still don't know"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Two years is concrete",
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "Three years each is harsh but even",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "there's this churning in me I can't put a name to"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Five years against three is a big difference for me. Against that, they'd go from free to serving time",
    "ae_welfare_concern": "they'd go from free to serving time, and I don't take that lightly",
    "pda_emotion_identification_difficulty": "I can't say what emotion is behind the knots"
  }
]
